Generate a Reformat for residential rental inventory in Hong Kong, Greater China. Track advertised monthly rent in HKD for each listing. Emit the first observation, then emit only when the absolute difference between the current rent and the last emitted rent is at least HKD 500. Compare against the last emitted rent, not the preceding input row. A transition between null and non-null rent always emits; two null rents emit nothing.

Assign a revision number starting at 1 independently for each listing, incrementing only when a record is emitted. Copy the current rent and observation timestamp into each emitted record. Input is ordered by listing_ref,observed_at with strictly increasing timestamps per listing.

Input 0: listing_ref long non-null, advertised_rent_hkd decimal nullable, observed_at date non-null. Output 0: listing_ref long non-null, advertised_rent_hkd decimal nullable, revision_no long non-null, starts_at date non-null.

```ctl
//#CTL2
boolean seen = false;
long lastListing = 0L;
decimal lastEmittedRent = null;
long revision = 0L;

function integer transform() {
    decimal currentRent = $in.0.advertised_rent_hkd;
    boolean emitRecord = false;

    if (!seen || $in.0.listing_ref != lastListing) {
        seen = true;
        lastListing = $in.0.listing_ref;
        revision = 0L;
        emitRecord = true;
    } else if (currentRent == null) {
        emitRecord = lastEmittedRent != null;
    } else if (lastEmittedRent == null) {
        emitRecord = true;
    } else {
        decimal difference = currentRent - lastEmittedRent;
        emitRecord = difference >= 500 || difference <= -500;
    }

    if (!emitRecord) {
        return SKIP;
    }

    revision = revision + 1L;
    lastEmittedRent = currentRent;
    $out.0.listing_ref = $in.0.listing_ref;
    $out.0.advertised_rent_hkd = currentRent;
    $out.1.revision_no = revision;
    $out.0.starts_at = $in.0.observed_at;
    return ALL;
}
```

