The healthcare fraud-detection review export for claims processed in Belgium, the Netherlands, and Luxembourg. All monetary values are in EUR. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. withdrawn claim: when review_state equals "WITHDRAWN", export nothing.
2. invalid claim amount: when invoiced_eur < 0, export INVALID (-invoiced_eur).
3. verified match: when invoiced_eur equals allowable_eur and provider_register_ref is not null, export CLEARED (0).
4. verification needed: when provider_register_ref is null or review_state equals "UNVERIFIED", export VERIFY (invoiced_eur).
5. investigated excess: when invoiced_eur > allowable_eur and investigation_open, export INVOICED (invoiced_eur) followed by ALLOWABLE (-allowable_eur) followed by EXPOSURE (invoiced_eur-allowable_eur).
6. minor excess: when invoiced_eur > allowable_eur and invoiced_eur-allowable_eur < 25, export WATCH (invoiced_eur-allowable_eur).
7. below allowance: when invoiced_eur < allowable_eur, export BELOW_ALLOWANCE (allowable_eur-invoiced_eur).
8. recovery review: when otherwise, export EXPOSURE (invoiced_eur-allowable_eur) followed by RECOVERY_RESERVE ((invoiced_eur-allowable_eur)/10).

Input 0 (In_benelux_claim_review_0): long[required] claim_key; string[required] review_state; decimal[required] invoiced_eur; decimal[required] allowable_eur; boolean[required] investigation_open; string[nullable] provider_register_ref.
Output 0 (Out_benelux_claim_review_0): long[required] claim_reference; string[required] review_entry; decimal[required] exposure_eur.
Each source ID is unique; carry claim_key into claim_reference. Entry labels go in review_entry, values in exposure_eur.

```ctl
//#CTL2

integer rule;

function integer count() {
    if ($in.0.review_state == "WITHDRAWN") {
        rule = 1;
        return 0;
    }
    if ($in.0.invoiced_eur < 0) {
        rule = 2;
        return 1;
    }
    if ($in.0.invoiced_eur == $in.0.allowable_eur && !isnull($in.0.provider_register_ref)) {
        rule = 3;
        return 1;
    }
    if (isnull($in.0.provider_register_ref) || $in.0.review_state == "UNVERIFIED") {
        rule = 4;
        return 1;
    }
    if ($in.0.invoiced_eur > $in.0.allowable_eur && $in.0.investigation_open) {
        rule = 5;
        return 3;
    }
    if ($in.0.invoiced_eur > $in.0.allowable_eur && $in.0.invoiced_eur - $in.0.allowable_eur < 25) {
        rule = 6;
        return 1;
    }
    if ($in.0.invoiced_eur < $in.0.allowable_eur) {
        rule = 7;
        return 1;
    }
    rule = 8;
    return 2;
}

function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.claim_reference = $in.0.claim_key;
    if (rule == 2) {
        $out.0.review_entry = "INVALID";
        $out.0.exposure_eur = -$in.0.invoiced_eur;
    } else if (rule == 3) {
        $out.0.review_entry = "CLEARED";
        $out.0.exposure_eur = 0;
    } else if (rule == 4) {
        $out.0.review_entry = "VERIFY";
        $out.0.exposure_eur = $in.0.invoiced_eur;
    } else if (rule == 5) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.review_entry = "INVOICED";
            $out.0.exposure_eur = $in.0.invoiced_eur;
        } else if (idx == 1) {
            $out.1.review_entry = "ALLOWABLE";
            $out.0.exposure_eur = -$in.0.allowable_eur;
        } else {
            $out.0.review_entry = "EXPOSURE";
            $out.0.exposure_eur = $in.0.invoiced_eur - $in.0.allowable_eur;
        }
    } else if (rule == 6) {
        $out.0.review_entry = "WATCH";
        $out.0.exposure_eur = $in.0.invoiced_eur - $in.0.allowable_eur;
    } else if (rule == 7) {
        $out.0.review_entry = "BELOW_ALLOWANCE";
        $out.0.exposure_eur = $in.0.allowable_eur - $in.0.invoiced_eur;
    } else if (rule == 8) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.review_entry = "EXPOSURE";
            $out.0.exposure_eur = $in.0.invoiced_eur - $in.0.allowable_eur;
        } else {
            $out.0.review_entry = "RECOVERY_RESERVE";
            $out.0.exposure_eur = ($in.0.invoiced_eur - $in.0.allowable_eur) / 10;
        }
    } else {
        return SKIP;
    }
    return OK;
}
