The employee scheduling adjustment export for a real estate agency in Japan. All durations are in minutes. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. cancelled assignment: when booking_state equals "CANCELLED" or requested_minutes equals 0, export nothing.
2. invalid allocation: when allocated_minutes < 0, export ERROR (-allocated_minutes).
3. fully covered assignment: when requested_minutes equals allocated_minutes, export nothing.
4. training assignment: when booking_state equals "TRAINING", export TRAINING (requested_minutes).
5. approved coverage shortage: when requested_minutes > allocated_minutes and manager_approved, export COVERED (allocated_minutes) followed by EXTRA (requested_minutes-allocated_minutes) followed by APPROVAL (0).
6. missing branch assignment: when branch_code is null and requested_minutes > allocated_minutes, export NEEDS_BRANCH (requested_minutes-allocated_minutes).
7. large coverage shortage: when requested_minutes-allocated_minutes > 120, export STANDARD_EXTRA (120) followed by ESCALATION (requested_minutes-allocated_minutes-120).
8. remaining adjustment: otherwise, export ADJUSTMENT (requested_minutes-allocated_minutes).

Input 0 (In_property_staffing_0): long column assignment_key, nulls forbidden
integer column requested_minutes, nulls forbidden
boolean column manager_approved, nulls forbidden
string column booking_state, nulls forbidden
integer column allocated_minutes, nulls forbidden
string column branch_code, nulls allowed.
Output 0 (Out_property_staffing_0): long column assignment_reference, nulls forbidden
string column schedule_entry, nulls forbidden
integer column duration_minutes, nulls forbidden.
