A legal-services claim settlement export for a UAE legal expenses provider. All monetary values are in AED. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom; apply only the first matching rule. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry. Emit entries in the stated order.

1. withdrawn claim: when claim_route equals "WITHDRAWN", export nothing.
2. invalid court outlay: when court_outlay < 0, export ERROR (-court_outlay).
3. missing evidence: when evidence_reference is null, export REVIEW (counsel_fee+court_outlay).
4. fee recovery: when counsel_fee < 0, export RECOVERY (counsel_fee+court_outlay).
5. verified negotiated claim: when claim_route equals "NEGOTIATED" and panel_verified is true, export LEGAL (counsel_fee*90/100) followed by COURT (court_outlay) followed by VERIFICATION (0).
6. pro bono representation: when claim_route equals "PRO_BONO", export COURT (court_outlay).
7. negotiated claim: when claim_route equals "NEGOTIATED", export LEGAL (counsel_fee*90/100) followed by COURT (court_outlay).
8. standard claim: otherwise, export SETTLEMENT (counsel_fee+court_outlay).

Input 0 (In_legal_claim_settlement_0): claim_number => required, long
counsel_fee => required, decimal
panel_verified => required, boolean
claim_route => required, string
court_outlay => required, decimal
evidence_reference => nullable, string.
Output 0 (Out_legal_claim_settlement_0): claim_reference => required, long
settlement_entry => required, string
aed_value => required, decimal.
Each source ID is unique; carry claim_number into claim_reference. Entry labels go in settlement_entry, values in aed_value.

```ctl
//#CTL2

function integer settlementRule() {
    if ($in.0.claim_route == "WITHDRAWN") return 1;
    if ($in.0.court_outlay < 0) return 2;
    if (isnull($in.0.evidence_reference)) return 3;
    if ($in.0.counsel_fee < 0) return 4;
    if ($in.0.claim_route == "NEGOTIATED" && $in.0.panel_verified) return 5;
    if ($in.0.claim_route == "PRO_BONO") return 6;
    if ($in.0.claim_route == "NEGOTIATED") return 7;
    return 8;
}

function integer count() {
    integer rule = settlementRule();
    if (rule == 1) return 0;
    if (rule == 5) return 3;
    if (rule == 7) return 2;
    return 1;
}

function integer transform(integer idx) {
    integer rule = settlementRule();
    if (rule == 1) return SKIP;

    $out.0.claim_reference = $in.0.claim_number;

    if (rule == 2) {
        $out.0.settlement_entry = "ERROR";
        $out.0.aed_value = -$in.0.court_outlay;
    } else if (rule == 3) {
        $out.0.settlement_entry = "REVIEW";
        $out.0.aed_value = $in.0.counsel_fee + $in.0.court_outlay;
    } else if (rule == 4) {
        $out.0.settlement_entry = "RECOVERY";
        $out.0.aed_value = $in.0.counsel_fee + $in.0.court_outlay;
    } else if (rule == 5 || rule == 7) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.settlement_entry = "LEGAL";
            $out.0.aed_value = $in.0.counsel_fee * 90 / 100;
        } else if (idx == 1) {
            $out.0.settlement_entry = "COURT";
            $out.0.aed_value = $in.0.court_outlay;
        } else {
            $out.0.settlement_entry = "VERIFICATION";
            $out.0.aed_value = 0;
        }
    } else if (rule == 6) {
        $out.0.settlement_entry = "COURT";
        $out.1.aed_value = $in.0.court_outlay;
    } else {
        $out.0.settlement_entry = "SETTLEMENT";
        $out.0.aed_value = $in.0.counsel_fee + $in.0.court_outlay;
    }
    return OK;
}
