The aircraft-parts procurement settlement export for a Polish airline operating in Eastern Europe. All monetary values are in PLN. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. incomplete or void purchase: when order_state equals "VOID" or supplier_invoice is null, export nothing.
2. invalid prepayment: when prepaid_pln < 0, export ERROR (-prepaid_pln).
3. fully settled purchase: when billed_pln equals prepaid_pln, export nothing.
4. cancelled purchase: when order_state equals "CANCELLED", export RELEASE (-prepaid_pln).
5. approved overpayment reconciliation: when prepaid_pln > billed_pln and finance_approved, export INVOICE (billed_pln) followed by PREPAYMENT (-prepaid_pln) followed by REVIEW (0).
6. procurement budget breach: when billed_pln-prepaid_pln > 10000, export BUDGET (10000) followed by OVER_BUDGET (billed_pln-prepaid_pln-10000).
7. recoverable overpayment: when prepaid_pln > billed_pln, export RECOVERABLE (prepaid_pln-billed_pln).
8. remaining payable: otherwise, export PAYABLE (billed_pln-prepaid_pln).

Input 0 (In_airline_procurement_0): long column purchase_key, nulls forbidden
decimal column billed_pln, nulls forbidden
boolean column finance_approved, nulls forbidden
string column order_state, nulls forbidden
decimal column prepaid_pln, nulls forbidden
string column supplier_invoice, nulls allowed.
Output 0 (Out_airline_procurement_0): long column purchase_ref, nulls forbidden
