The supplier settlement export for an automotive procurement team in Greater China. This export covers mainland China component purchases, with all monetary values in CNY. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. withheld invoice: when clearance_code is null or equals "CANCELLED", export nothing.
2. invalid credit: when credit_cny < 0, export ERROR (-credit_cny).
3. fully offset invoice: when invoice_cny equals credit_cny, export CLEARED (0).
4. provisional settlement: when clearance_code equals "PROVISIONAL", export PROVISIONAL (invoice_cny-credit_cny).
5. verified supplier credit surplus: when credit_cny > invoice_cny and vat_verified, export INVOICE (invoice_cny) followed by CREDIT (-credit_cny) followed by VAT_CHECK (0).
6. small payable balance: when invoice_cny > credit_cny and invoice_cny-credit_cny < 100, export SMALL_PAYABLE (invoice_cny-credit_cny).
7. supplier credit balance: when credit_cny > invoice_cny, export CREDIT_BALANCE (invoice_cny-credit_cny).
8. standard payable: otherwise, export PAYMENT ((invoice_cny-credit_cny)*0.9) followed by QUALITY_RETENTION ((invoice_cny-credit_cny)*0.1).

