Please map these incoming records.

Process spare-part requisitions at an electricity utility warehouse in the United Arab Emirates. All counts represent individual spare parts.

Copy request_key. Trim asset_tag; classify null or empty as ABSENT, a whole-string mismatch to AE[0-9]{6} as MALFORMED, otherwise ACCEPTED. Output this classification as tag_check. Also output clean_tag as the trimmed uppercase text, using an empty string for null. Validate the pattern against the trimmed text before uppercasing.

Output quarantine_active from quarantine_mark, treating null as false. rack_ready means rack_location is nonblank after trimming. technician_ready means technician_badge matches the exact whole-string pattern UT[0-9]{3}; null does not match.

Count one issue for each of these five conditions:
- tag_check is not ACCEPTED.
- available_units is null or negative.
- requested_units is null or nonpositive.
- Either rack_ready or technician_ready is false. Count only one issue even if both are false.
- quarantine_active is true.

Set handling_lane to INSPECTION if any issue exists; otherwise REPLENISH if requested_units exceeds available_units; otherwise DISPATCH.

Set stock_class to UNKNOWN for null available_units, EMPTY at <=0, BULK at >=100, and SMALL otherwise.

Set coverage_class to UNKNOWN if either count is null; otherwise INVALID if available_units is negative or requested_units is nonpositive; otherwise SHORT if requested_units exceeds available_units; otherwise COVERED.

