A mining compliance and audit ledger export for Moroccan quarry reporting in North Africa. Quantities are whole tonnes. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry. Preserve the stated entry order.

1. withdrawn declaration: when filing_class equals "WITHDRAWN", export nothing.
2. invalid declared tonnage: when declared_tonnes < 0, export DATA_ERROR (-declared_tonnes).
3. missing extraction permit: when permit_code is null or equals "", export PERMIT_REVIEW (declared_tonnes) followed by COMPLIANCE_ALERT (0).
4. excess extraction: when surveyed_tonnes > declared_tonnes, export UNDECLARED (surveyed_tonnes-declared_tonnes) followed by ASSESSED (surveyed_tonnes).
5. exempt filing: when filing_class equals "EXEMPT", export nothing.
6. high-volume audit: when declared_tonnes+surveyed_tonnes >= 200 and audit_selected, export DECLARED (declared_tonnes) followed by VERIFIED (surveyed_tonnes) followed by AUDIT_MARKER (0).
7. annual reconciliation: when filing_class equals "ANNUAL", export DECLARED (declared_tonnes) followed by VERIFIED (surveyed_tonnes).
8. routine review: otherwise, export VARIANCE (declared_tonnes-surveyed_tonnes).

Input 0 (In_quarry_filing_0): filing_number:long (required); filing_class:string (required); declared_tonnes:long (required); surveyed_tonnes:long (required); audit_selected:boolean (required); permit_code:string (nullable).
Output 0 (Out_quarry_compliance_0): declaration_ref:long (required); ledger_category:string (required); tonnage_value:long (required).
Each source ID is unique; carry filing_number into declaration_ref. Entry labels go in ledger_category, values in tonnage_value. surveyed_tonnes is always nonnegative.

```ctl
//#CTL2

function integer filingRule() {
    if ($in.0.filing_class == "WITHDRAWN") return 1;
    if ($in.0.declared_tonnes <= 0) return 2;
    if (isnull($in.0.permit_code) || $in.0.permit_code == "") return 3;
    if ($in.0.surveyed_tonnes > $in.0.declared_tonnes) return 4;
    if ($in.0.filing_class == "EXEMPT") return 5;
    // Equivalent to sum >= 200 without overflowing a long sum.
    if ($in.0.declared_tonnes >= 200 - $in.0.surveyed_tonnes && $in.0.audit_selected) return 6;
    if ($in.0.filing_class == "ANNUAL") return 7;
    return 8;
}

function integer count() {
    integer rule = filingRule();
    if (rule == 1 || rule == 5) return 0;
    if (rule == 3 || rule == 4 || rule == 7) return 2;
    if (rule == 6) return 3;
    return 1;
}

function integer transform(integer idx) {
    integer rule = filingRule();
    $out.0.declaration_ref = $in.0.filing_number;
    if (rule == 2) {
        $out.0.ledger_category = "DATA_ERROR";
        $out.0.tonnage_value = -$in.0.declared_tonnes;
    } else if (rule == 3) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "PERMIT_REVIEW";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = $in.0.declared_tonnes;
        } else {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "COMPLIANCE_ALERT";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = 0;
        }
    } else if (rule == 4) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "UNDECLARED";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = $in.0.surveyed_tonnes - $in.0.declared_tonnes;
        } else {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "ASSESSED";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = $in.0.surveyed_tonnes;
        }
    } else if (rule == 6 || rule == 7) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "DECLARED";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = $in.0.declared_tonnes;
        } else if (idx == 1) {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "VERIFIED";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = $in.0.surveyed_tonnes;
        } else {
            $out.0.ledger_category = "AUDIT_MARKER";
            $out.0.tonnage_value = 0;
        }
    } else {
        $out.0.ledger_category = "VARIANCE";
        $out.0.tonnage_value = $in.0.declared_tonnes - $in.0.surveyed_tonnes;
    }
    return ALL;
}
