The Benelux public transit asset maintenance allocations export for tram and metro depots. All monetary amounts are in EUR. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. cancelled work order: when work_state equals "CANCELLED", export nothing.
2. invalid spending limit: when spending_limit < 0, export ERROR (-spending_limit).
3. missing safety clearance: when clearance_code is null, export SAFETY_HOLD (estimated_cost).
4. supplier credit: when work_state equals "CREDIT", export CREDIT (-estimated_cost).
5. audited joint maintenance: when work_state equals "JOINT" and audit_needed is true, export DEPOT (estimated_cost*40/100) followed by CONTRACTOR (estimated_cost*60/100) followed by AUDIT (0).
6. over budget: when estimated_cost > spending_limit, export BUDGET_HOLD (estimated_cost-spending_limit).
7. joint maintenance: when work_state equals "JOINT", export DEPOT (estimated_cost*40/100) followed by CONTRACTOR (estimated_cost*60/100).
8. local maintenance: otherwise, export MAINTENANCE (estimated_cost).

Input 0 (In_transit_maintenance_0): work_order_number: type=long, required
estimated_cost: type=decimal, required
audit_needed: type=boolean, required
work_state: type=string, required
spending_limit: type=long, required
clearance_code: type=string, nullable.
Output 0 (Out_transit_maintenance_0): maintenance_ref: type=long, required
allocation_kind: type=string, required
eur_amount: type=decimal, required.
Each source ID is unique; carry work_order_number into maintenance_ref. Entry labels go in allocation_kind, values in eur_amount.

```ctl
//#CTL2

// Rule number selected for the current source record.
integer rule = 0;

function integer count() {
    if ($in.0.work_state == "CANCELLED") {
        rule = 1;
        return 0;
    }
    if ($in.0.spending_limit < 0) {
        rule = 2;
        return 1;
    }
    if (isnull($in.0.clearance_code)) {
        rule = 3;
        return 1;
    }
    if ($in.0.work_state == "CREDIT") {
        rule = 4;
        return 1;
    }
    if ($in.0.work_state == "JOINT" && $in.0.audit_needed) {
        rule = 5;
        return 3;
    }
    if ($in.0.estimated_cost > $in.0.spending_limit) {
        rule = 6;
        return 1;
    }
    if ($in.0.work_state == "JOINT") {
        rule = 7;
        return 2;
    }
    rule = 8;
    return 1;
}

function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.maintenance_ref = $in.0.work_order_number;

    if (rule == 2) {
        $out.0.allocation_kind = "ERROR";
        // Convert before negating to avoid long minimum-value overflow.
        decimal limitAmount = $in.0.spending_limit;
        $out.0.eur_amount = -limitAmount;
    } else if (rule == 3) {
        $out.0.allocation_kind = "SAFETY_HOLD";
        $out.0.eur_amount = $in.0.estimated_cost;
    } else if (rule == 4) {
        $out.0.allocation_kind = "CREDIT";
        $out.0.eur_amount = -$in.0.estimated_cost;
    } else if (rule == 5 || rule == 7) {
        if (idx == 0) {
            $out.0.allocation_kind = "DEPOT";
            $out.0.eur_amount = $in.0.estimated_cost * 40 / 100;
        } else if (idx == 1) {
            $out.0.allocation_kind = "CONTRACTOR";
            $out.0.eur_amount = $in.0.estimated_cost * 60 / 100;
        } else {
            $out.0.allocation_kind = "AUDIT";
            $out.0.eur_amount = 0;
        }
    } else if (rule == 6) {
        $out.0.allocation_kind = "BUDGET_HOLD";
        $out.0.eur_amount = $in.0.estimated_cost - $in.0.spending_limit;
    } else {
        $out.0.allocation_kind = "MAINTENANCE";
        $out.0.eur_amount = $in.0.estimated_cost;
    }
    return OK;
}
